        "id": 1072905
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T07:31:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this section is a bit vague as it does not say what a contributor must actually do in this case.\n\nFor example, suppose a developer uses an AI assistant to generate most of a new Java class, carefully reviews and modifies it, and submits the change under their own name.\n\nIs that compliant without explicitly disclosing the AI assistance? \n\nI think we should explicitly state whether AI usage must be disclosed and, if so, where: commit message, change description, etc.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 129,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "d936dee47d0f001cea35abca1c9e5ba78a76d543",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a91ac1dc_f1911c63",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1072905
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T07:31:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we actually require every patch set to be manually submitted?\n\nFor example, a developer could review and validate a generated change and then have a script push it to Gerrit. That doesn\u0027t make the contribution any less accountable.\n\nI think the important distinction is whether the change has been reviewed and validated by a human, rather than whether the actual upload was manual.\n\nCould we focus on prohibiting autonomous changes without human involvement, rather than prohibiting automated submissions in general? That would also avoid needing specific exceptions for CI/CD and release scripts, etc.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 142,
        "startChar": 66,
        "endLine": 143,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "d936dee47d0f001cea35abca1c9e5ba78a76d543",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e6bfbde_3b7945a5",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1072905
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T07:31:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"Total and unconditional liability\" sounds like contributors would be responsible for anything that goes wrong with their code, even bugs or issues discovered long after the contribution was merged.\n\nI was reading the CLA [1], and in Section 6 it states: \n```\n[...]\nYou provide Your Contributions on an \"AS IS\" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, \neither express or implied.\n[...]\n```\n\nI think we should phrase it so that contributors are held responsible for understanding and reviewing their changes, rather than implying unlimited liability in general.\n\n\n[1] https://cla.developers.google.com/about/google-individual",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "d936dee47d0f001cea35abca1c9e5ba78a76d543",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d81b1ebd_67f634dc",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 165,
      "author": {
        "id": 1072905
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T07:31:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we actually require DCO sign-off for Gerrit contributions?\n\nAs far as I understand, we require the Google CLA, but we don\u0027t generally require contributors to add a `Signed-off-by:` footer.\n\nI found documentation explaining what the DCO is [1], but there is nothing in the Contribution Guidelines [2].\n\nThis seems to introduce an additional requirement that isn\u0027t part of our current contribution process. Could we clarify whether that\u0027s intentional? Otherwise, I would avoid mentioning DCO compliance here.\n\n[1] https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/Documentation/user-signedoffby.html\n[2] https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/Documentation/dev-contributing.html",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 165,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 165,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "d936dee47d0f001cea35abca1c9e5ba78a76d543",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01dd55ea_cc569655",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 165,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054778
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T12:18:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1\n\nThat would require a process change and should be introduced and documented. Furthermore, it would require a configuration change to enforce it AFAIK.",
      "parentUuid": "d81b1ebd_67f634dc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 165,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 165,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "d936dee47d0f001cea35abca1c9e5ba78a76d543",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
