    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d09e4d0_c5a895cc",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T15:33:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The point here is responsibility: you are submitting the code, and therefore you are responsible for it.\nIf you are unsure about any of the tools you are using, think twice before using them.\n\nAdding `Assisted-By: Claude` and then lifting any responsibility for potential copyright infringement is explicitly against the Google CLA and therefore should not be accepted.\n\nI can refer to the Google CLA here and add \"you are aware of\"to avoid any potential confusion. Nevertheless, you, the author, provide your code and are liable for any copyright infringement.\n\nWhen I personally use AI, I never include the output as the LLM spits it out without having gone through a careful analysis of the sources.\nMany times, after a deep investigation, I have found that the sources were misrepresented and the deductions made by AI were unreliable and therefore not trusted enough to be included.\n\nOf course, the due diligence cannot be perfect; I agree. However, it must lie on the author\u0027s side and not the reviewer\u0027s.\n\nI personally feel that allowing people to just _contribute anything_ with superficial due diligence, and then adding the requirement to include `Assisted-By: Claude` or similar, would increase the workload for reviewers. \n\nLet me know if the amended wording works for you.",
      "parentUuid": "22e6629e_97eafd17",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 66
